{
  "note": "The word list of record for this repo's Simplified Technical English rules. `ste-lint.mjs` reads this file, and `docs/style_ste.md` documents it. Do not copy entries into prose — a second copy goes stale and then lies.",
  "basedOn": "ASD-STE100 Issue 9 (released 2025-01-15), Part 2 (the not-approved word list). Paraphrased and cut down to the words that occur in software documentation. This file is NOT the standard and does not reproduce it. ASD owns ASD-STE100; get the free official copy at https://www.asd-ste100.org/.",
  "tiers": {
    "notApproved": "An error in BOTH tiers. Each word has a plain replacement that loses no meaning.",
    "strictOnly": "An error in STRICT files, a warning in INFORMED files. These words carry hedging or connective nuance that rationale prose is allowed to keep.",
    "technicalAllowed": "Technical Names and Technical Verbs (ASD-STE100 permits both even when they are not in the approved dictionary). Listed here so a project word is never reported. Add to this list rather than weakening a rule."
  },
  "formRules": "`verb: true` also matches the -s, -ed and -ing forms (final -e is dropped before -ed/-ing). `forms` adds any others, such as a doubled consonant or a noun form.",

